  "summary": "Preprints replace variational loops with gated fixed feature maps, Riemannian flows or RL training, and bound observables reachable by fixed-readout QNNs.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is reducing reliance on standard variational optimization of quantum neural networks while clarifying what these models can represent. Soft-MoQE uses a classical gating network to mix fixed quantum feature maps, avoiding variational quantum training, and matches trainable QNNs on MNIST. An autonomous scheme based on Riemannian gradients removes measurements and classical feedback from the training loop. A fully quantum Transformer combines SVD-based non-unitary circuits with quantum nonlinear activations and is trained by multi-agent RL without backpropagation. On expressivity, contractive layers add all-to-all couplings with a single trainable parameter on Rydberg arrays. A separate analysis characterizes the effective observables reachable by fixed-readout QNNs under unitary, mixed-unitary and CPTP resources and proves strict inclusions between these classes. Related work uses ML to extrapolate gate, measurement and reset syntax for scaling holographic circuits. Applications include QFT-based hybrid PointNet models for LiDAR classification and a quantum-inspired spiking VAE for LHC di-jet anomaly detection. All works are preprints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
